    "problem_statement": "Required option not working correctly with empty values\n\n```\n>>> from textfsm import TextFSM\n>>> import io\n>>> tplt = 'Value Required boo (one)\\nValue Filldown hoo (two)\\n\\nStart\\n  ^$boo -> Next.Record\\n  ^$hoo -> Next.Record\\n\\nEOF\\n'\n>>> t = TextFSM(io.StringIO(tplt))\n>>> data = 'two\\none'\n>>> result = t.ParseText(data)\n>>> result\n[['one', 'two']]\n>>> \n>>> # Now let's try with an empty value\n>>> tplt = 'Value Required boo (one)\\nValue Filldown hoo (two)\\n\\nStart\\n  ^$boo -> Next.Record\\n  ^$hoo -> Next.Record\\n\\nEOF\\n'\n>>> t = TextFSM(io.StringIO(tplt))\n>>> data = 'two\\n'  # No value for 'boo'\n>>> result = t.ParseText(data)\n>>> result\n[['', 'two']]  # Should not record this row since 'boo' is Required but empty\n```\n\nThe `Required` option is not working correctly. When a value is marked as `Required`, empty values should cause the record to be skipped, but currently empty values are being recorded.\n\nThis also affects other tests like `List` and `Continue` options when combined with `Required`.\n\nI think the issue is in the `OnSaveRecord` method in the `Required` class. It seems to be checking for `None` instead of empty values."
